Gavin77 wrote:
> You dont need to drop them on the ground for the pet to eat ? I tried
> to throw them to the pet, but the game does not let me throw food.
Erm, actually you *can* throw food.  If you hit * instead of ? at any 
inventory prompt, you get a list of everything, not just obviously 
sensible things.  You can also just hit the letter if you know it.  I 
don't think dropping them on the ground helps much.  You use treats 
(tripe and meatballs for both cats and dogs, apples and carrots for 
horses) to acquire new pets and to train your pets to steal thing from 
shops, by throwing the treat to the pet.  Having a treat in your 
inventory will merely make the pet follow you more.

See the pet spoiler for more details and corrections to anything wrong I 
have said:

http://www.statslab.cam.ac.uk/~eva/nethack/spoilerlist.html

